# Universal Screens — let the host create a virtual keyboard/mouse.
#
# The host injects the phone's keystrokes through the kernel's uinput device
# (see crates/host-linux/src/inject.rs for why uinput and not XTEST or the XDG
# RemoteDesktop portal). /dev/uinput is root-owned by default, so without this
# rule the app runs, accepts a connection, reports "connected" — and moves
# nothing. That silent failure is the reason the host checks the permission on
# startup and shows this file's contents when it isn't satisfied.
#
# Install:
#   sudo cp installer/99-universal-screens-uinput.rules /etc/udev/rules.d/
#   sudo usermod -aG input $USER
#   sudo udevadm control --reload-rules && sudo udevadm trigger
#
# Then LOG OUT AND BACK IN — group membership is established at login, so the
# rule appears to have done nothing until you do.
#
# static_node=uinput matters as much as the mode: on most systems the uinput
# module is not loaded until something asks for it, and the device node has to
# exist with the right ownership *before* the first open, not after.
KERNEL=="uinput", GROUP="input", MODE="0660", OPTIONS+="static_node=uinput"
